# Keep Unix line endings everywhere, whatever machine checks the code out.
#
# Git on Windows helpfully converts files to Windows line endings. That breaks
# a Dockerfile whose commands continue across lines with a backslash: the
# container build fails with an error that says nothing about line endings, on
# a machine where everything looks correct. This is cheaper than that afternoon.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch what is inside an image or an archive.
*.png binary
*.db binary
*.ged text eol=lf
